     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Blocking h1_2:escalate and h1_1:access (or h3_0:obtain) makes crown:obtain unreachable, and no single block can. With h1_2 blocked, h3_2 and h2_1 cannot be reached. That cuts h3_1, h4_1, h4_2, h5_0 and h5_2. h5_1 is still reachable through h3_0, which comes from h1_1 (an AND of the two entry footholds). Blocking h1_1 or h3_0 as well cuts it. One block is not enough because h5_1 has two independent routes: h3_0 via h1_1, and h3_2 via h1_2. No single blockable step lies on both, and h5_1 itself is not enough since h5_0 and h5_2 remain. So the minimum is 2.\"}"
    }
